From: "Barak A. Pearlmutter" <barak+git@pearlmutter.net>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 13:35:00 +0100
Subject: fix regressions from the port to new-style connect

The port from SIGNAL/SLOT to functor-based connect() in 2.1.3.1
introduced two regressions.

MainWindow::updateViews(int index=-1) treats its argument as an index
into the page-pair combobox.  The old string-based connections called
updateViews() with no argument, but the functor-based ones forward the
int (or bool) argument of the signal, so changing e.g. the zoom to 186%
jumped to the 186th differing page pair, or did nothing at all if there
were fewer pairs.  Only viewDiffComboBox should pass its index.

The options dialog stored the pen and brush styles in the comboboxes as
QBrush values, but read them back with QVariant::toInt(), which yields
0 (Qt::NoPen and Qt::NoBrush) for a QBrush.  Changing either combobox
therefore set both styles to "none", which disables the OK button.
Store the style as an int, as 2.1.3 did.

Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/1041494
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/1051422
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/1094167
Forwarded: no
